&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to revolutionize healthcare, making it faster and more accessible than ever before?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we started:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2013 by Dwayne D’Souza,&amp;nbsp;HeliosX&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;was built on a simple but powerful idea: healthcare should be easier to access, faster to receive, and centred around the individual. From day one, we’ve grown without external funding; scaling profitably through technology, disciplined execution, and deep medical expertise. What started as a challenger idea has become one of the most significant healthcare platforms operating globally today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where we are now:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’ve earned the trust of millions of people worldwide through category-leading products and well-known brands, including MedExpress, Dermatica, ZipHealth, RocketRX, and Levity. A key driver of our success is vertical integration; we operate our own manufacturing and proprietary products, led by in-house medical teams, researchers, and pharmacists at the top of their fields.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2025, HeliosX treated more than 1.7 million patients globally and reached £781m in revenue, representing +337% year-on-year growth and cementing our position as the clear market leader in the UK. That growth translates into real-world outcomes: our weight-loss treatments helped patients lose 8.5 million kilograms of excess weight in 2025 alone, contributing to an estimated 1,300 fewer cardiac events. This is growth with measurable, life-changing impact at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, we operate across four international markets, with successful launches in Germany and Canada and continued expansion in the US. We were also recently recognised in the Sunday Times Top 100 fastest-growing tech companies, further validation of both our momentum and our ambition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where we’re going:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2026 is another significant year for HeliosX. Our ambition is to surpass £1.1bn in revenue, continue expanding thoughtfully into new international markets and broaden our condition and treatment portfolio. As we scale, we&#39;re focused on building the technology, operational excellence and clinical capabilities that will support sustainable long-term growth. Joining HeliosX now means helping shape the systems, teams and products that will define the next chapter of digital healthcare. You&#39;ll be solving complex problems at pace, working alongside exceptional people and building products that genuinely improve lives at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There’s never been a more exciting time to join HeliosX. Come be a part of making our dream of easier and faster healthcare a reality!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We&#39;re&amp;nbsp;looking for an exceptional Senior Compounding Pharmacist to lead our sterile and non-sterile operations within the Lab in Leamington Spa. This is a rare opportunity to join a forward-thinking organisation dedicated to delivering high-quality, treatments while maintaining the highest standards of patient safety, regulatory compliance, and pharmaceutical excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our&amp;nbsp;Senior Compounding Pharmacist, you will take ownership of the safe, compliant, and efficient compounding of treatments across both sterile and non-sterile operations. You’ll be at the heart of our compounding facility, ensuring every preparation meets rigorous GPhC standards and aligns with MHRA, EMA, ICH, and ISO guidance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is far more than a traditional pharmacy position. You’ll combine hands-on pharmacist leadership within our Lab environment with day-to-day production and laboratory management, driving operational excellence across the entire compounding process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based at our Leamington Spa Hub within the Laboratory, working Monday-Friday 9am-5pm.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compounding &amp;amp; Clinical Oversight&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee sterile and non-sterile compounding processes, including preparation, dispensing, and labelling of compounded medications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sterile compounding operations, ensuring cleanroom protocols, sanitation, daily logs, calibration, and hazardous waste disposal are properly maintained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and document product/batch verification and quality assurance checks to safeguard safety, efficacy, and sterility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and continually update SOPs for sterile and non-sterile compounding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the care team to support safe, effective treatment, counselling patients and answering inquiries as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document and report medication errors, near-misses, or patient concerns, driving continuous quality improvement (CQI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide global support by collaborating with HeliosX&#39;s international compounding teams (including the US) on formulation updates and stability studies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Production &amp;amp; Lab Management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create weekly production plans, assign compounding tasks to technicians, and manage scheduling across multiple compounding areas to meet manufacturing demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report key production metrics, costs, and quality data to wider operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage all lab equipment and plant, scheduling preventive maintenance, break-fix response, and contingency planning for single points of failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage compounding consumables and related inventory, minimising holding costs while avoiding stock-outs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out root cause analyses of process failures and product write-offs, and lead related investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interrogate new processes and technical transfers for flaws, ensuring methods can be replicated reliably at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own documentation and change control systems, tracking reviews, approvals, and revisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People Management &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train, supervise and support all lab staff in compounding technique, compliance, and best practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Line manage the compounding/manufacturing team, capturing individual performance metrics and delivering feedback, development, and improvement plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as hiring manager for new team members and manage agency staff as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an ongoing training and competency programme, including assessments to score staff performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the correct pharmacist-to-technician ratio and a positive, efficient workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion housekeeping standards and drive adherence to cGMP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee compliance with GPhC standards and relevant guidance from MHRA, EMA, ICH, and ISO across sterile and non-sterile compounding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular audits and inspections, building and improving auditing tools to monitor process adherence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for and participate in regulatory inspections, ensuring full readiness and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and report on temperature testing and other quality controls across compounding operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate operational or dispatch issues promptly to the central operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active GPhC registration as a Pharmacist (required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2 years&#39; experience in sterile compounding; non-sterile compounding experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous supervisory or line management experience in a compounding or pharmaceutical manufacturing setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the formulation and compounding of complex sterile and non-sterile preparations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of pharmaceutical compounding quality standards, including Medicines Act 1968 (Section 10 exemptions), MHRA guidance on &quot;Specials&quot; and relevant GPhC regulatory frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in pharmaceutical formulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Skills:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing production planning, equipment, and inventory in a lab or manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented, with robust quality control, documentation, and root-cause analysis practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in personnel management, with strong leadership, training, and performance development capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to maintain regulatory compliance and manage inspections/audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator, able to counsel patients and collaborate with the integrated care team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving aptitude and a proactive approach to continuous quality improvement (CQI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why work with us?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At HeliosX, we want to improve healthcare for everyone, and to do this we need a team of brilliant people who share that ambition. We are currently a diverse team of engineers, scientists, clinical researchers, physicians, pharmacists, marketeers, and customer care specialists committed to our mission - but we need more talented folks to join us, if we want to achieve our global ambitions!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aside from working with our all-star team, here are the other benefits of coming on board:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday plus UK Bank Holidays&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private health insurance, along with extra dental and eye care cover&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle-to-work Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electric Car Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Dermatica and MedExpress products every month, as well as family discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Headspace subscription, discounted gym memberships, and a learning and development budget&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt; #LI-&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;I-Senior #LI-Onsite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;I-Senior #LI-Onsite&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Director, Growth Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Growth Marketing is a strategic leader responsible for marketing our flagship Playstation Plus subscription service, and Playstation’s multi-billion-dollar D2C businesses, Playstation Store and Playstation Direct.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting directly to the SVP, Marketing, this role is an integral part of the Playstation Marketing Leadership team and will oversee future growth initiatives at the intersection of digital services, experiences, or community. This individual will lead a geographically dispersed team, driving world-class performance to ensure that it achieves its strategic objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize the revenue potential of Playstation DTC (Store / Direct) and Services (Plus) business lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own bottom-of-the-funnel conversion strategies across business lines and measure performance against business targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a globally dispersed team of growth marketers responsible for PlayStation Store, PlayStation Plus and PlayStation Direct marketing, leading direction on strategy, processes, measurement, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Marketing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the main lead of Marketing for the Store and Services business units, taking a key role on their leadership team by ensuring the full marketing offense – from insight to execution and evaluation – are strategically aligned and performed with excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Marketing input as the voice of the consumer on cross-functional strategic projects to create the future of PlayStation’s direct to consumer opportunity, inclusive of future product development roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the development of the annual strategic plan and budget recommendations to fuel the growth and success of the D2C businesses and ensure annual revenue and business performance targets are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Go-to-Market Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead go-to-market campaigns, with end-to-end accountability for targeting, positioning, and execution, with a strong focus on digital and performance tactics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage output from insights and analytics to develop a global view of PlayStation Store &amp;amp; Services consumers that informs marketing strategy and plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fuel the Playstation consumer flywheel to maximize player’s engagement and value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor player engagement and prioritize tactics to engage new players, retain existing player base, and reclaim inactive players on the platform. &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong working relationships with leaders across the Marketing organization and with global SIE teams, including Brand Marketing, International Marketing, Media, CRM, Marketing Technology, Marketing Analytics, Commercial Teams, Consumer Experience Product Marketing, Content, and Consumer Insights).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance global alignment with appropriate local and product-level flexibility, reinforcing a one SIE mindset while respecting market and portfolio needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage, recruit, develop, and retain a high-performance team that delivers against business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage understanding of cultural differences to influence actions and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain a positive culture built around open dialogue, mutual trust, respect, and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As you will be working closely with global teams, regular international travel may be required as well as a flexible approach to working hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Business, Marketing, Advertising, or a related discipline. Master’s degree, MBA, or equivalent experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven 12–15+ years of progressive marketing experience, including significant leadership experience within gaming, entertainment, technology, eCommerce, or other high-growth consumer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of developing and leading data-driven growth marketing strategies across acquisition, lifecycle, retention, engagement, and performance marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience within eCommerce-led businesses, ideally spanning both physical and digital products, services, or content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in delivering personalised, one-to-one consumer communications at scale, using customer data, segmentation, automation, and experimentation to drive measurable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of paid media and performance marketing, with experience partnering closely with internal media teams and external agencies to optimise investment and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or scaling subscription, membership, loyalty, and rewards programmes is highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of consumer behaviour and digital engagement, ideally gained within gaming, entertainment, technology, culture, or youth-focused brands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine interest in gaming, entertainment, technology, and evolving digital consumer behaviours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accomplished people leader with experience building, developing, and leading high-performing, multidisciplinary marketing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and analytical mindset, with the ability to translate customer, behavioural, and performance data into clear strategic priorities and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence senior executives and cross-functional leaders, align stakeholders around shared objectives, and drive decisions across complex global organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and interpersonal skills, with the judgement, adaptability, and leadership presence required to operate effectively in a fast-moving, highly collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary bonus opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid Working (within Flexmodes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dental Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days holiday per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On Site Gym&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidised Café&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free soft drinks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On site bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to cycle garage and showers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
